WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.495
Jake Gabbard: Crimes
have played a big role

00:00:10.495 --> 00:00:13.128
in many famous movies and TV shows,

00:00:13.128 --> 00:00:14.670
and of course, when there's a crime,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.680
there's also going to be punishment,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.180
and this usually means
someone is going to prison.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.420
When filmmakers need to
shoot a prison scene,

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.340
instead of recreating one
from scratch in a studio,

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.610
they can now film everything

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.710
at the Arthur Kill Correctional
Facility in New York,

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.910
which has been converted into

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.380
a fully functional production facility.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.200
We got an inside look at how
they turned what was once

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.103
a prison into a go-to set
for movie and TV production.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.010
Hey guys, we are here at

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.930
the Arthur Kill Correctional
Facility on Staten Island.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:52.763
This is where shows and movies

00:00:52.763 --> 00:00:54.600
like "Orange Is the New Black,"

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.370
"Daredevil," and "Ocean's
8" film their prison scenes.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.880
Let's go inside and take a look.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.180
But first, a little history.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.380
The former men's prison opened in 1976

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.560
and could hold 931 prisoners.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.350
Arthur Kill is the strip of
water between Staten Island

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.940
and New Jersey, which
is how it got its name.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.620
Governor Andrew Cuomo
closed the prison in 2011,

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.280
after which Broadway Stages
purchased the property,

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.080
leaving much of it intact.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.070
One of the most famous areas to shoot

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.980
is the front of the visitors' entrance

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.178
with its iconic guard tower.

00:01:27.178 --> 00:01:29.790
All along the watchtower.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.090
Where you can get a good
view of the grounds.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.660
Just overwatching the prison.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.100
Whoa, what are you doing over there?

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.275
Hold on!

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.040
This is where Sandra Bullock walks out

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.610
in the beginning of "Ocean's 8"

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.810
and where we see the inmates leaving

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.410
at the end of season six of
"Orange Is the New Black."

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:03.583
Piper: Oh, man!

00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:04.416
Jake: All right, so we're standing here

00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:06.500
in the visitors' area of the prison.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.240
This is where you come
in, you get signed in,

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.980
you get checked, get processed through,

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:10.920
and then they would lead you through

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.933
to meet up with your prisoner.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.850
All right, here you go, here's my stuff.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.320
Let's go.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.420
Let's go make a movie.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.560
Surrounding the facility is
the same barbed-wire fencing

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.140
from the prison to make it look authentic.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.500
Also authentic, the giant
keys that are still used

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.870
to lock up various parts of the building.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.070
This is what you want.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.793
This is the key to the SHU.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.390
These things are heavy-duty.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.660
Next on the tour was the visitation room,

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.430
where many crime dramas are typically set.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.580
Arthur Kill has an area
where you can meet at a table

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.020
or behind a thick pane of glass.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.580
To quote the great George Bluth,

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.960
"I may have committed minor treason."

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.060
When we visited, we noticed
several prop vending machines

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.400
left around the room.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.390
So like, as you can tell, this was a prop

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:04.880
because everything is turned backwards

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.450
'cause they can't show the logos.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.950
That being said, it looks
like there's a big raid

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.150
on the snacks in whatever
scene they were filming here

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.860
'cause it is slim pickings.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.590
But the pickings were even
slimmer in the kitchen.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.815
"Orange Is the New Black"
filmed season seven

00:03:17.815 --> 00:03:18.890
at Arthur Kill,

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.870
and they left behind
plenty of fake prop food.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:24.530
They say prison food is really
bad, but I bet prop prison

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.900
food is even worse 'cause it's not real.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.053
Foam taters.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:34.080
Connecting much of the prison
is an area called Broadway.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.760
It's this big, imposing
hallway where sets are built,

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.140
they're moved from one wing to another,

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.100
and when this was a prison,
this was the main stretch

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.530
that connected it all together.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.140
What was once the prison
gym has now been converted

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.760
into a huge soundstage,
which we couldn't film

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.300
because Hulu's "Wu-Tang: An American Saga"

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.930
was in production inside.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.620
There's also a chapel,
classrooms, and a greenhouse.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.300
While on tour, we noticed a really

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.330
heavy-duty-looking iron door,

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.544
which turned out to be a total fake.

00:04:03.544 --> 00:04:05.882
Let me outta here!

00:04:05.882 --> 00:04:07.272
Huh.

00:04:07.272 --> 00:04:08.105
Easy.

00:04:08.105 --> 00:04:11.270
But this door and area of the
prison might look familiar

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.320
since it was part of a huge escape scene

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.780
in Netflix's "Daredevil,"
which, of course,

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.653
we had to try and reenact.

00:04:20.032 --> 00:04:22.630
Loudspeaker: Code 33, code 33.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.030
Jake: Key sound, key sound.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.870
A "Daredevil" fight scene was also filmed

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:45.400
in the prison's medical center.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.810
We didn't get to see the
general-population cells,

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.560
but for "Orange Is the New Black,"

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.330
much of those scenes
are filmed at their set

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.940
at Astoria Kaufman Studios in Queens.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:57.063
The infamous SHU scene, however,
was filmed at the prison.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.490
Facing my fears, going to the SHU.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.540
Each cell was outfitted with beds,

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.800
a small sink, and a toilet.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.870
I could see why this is ideal
to make a show or a movie

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.430
because you are really immersing yourself

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:13.430
in that environment.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:15.580
While many TV shows and movies come here

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.310
for the prison aesthetic,
the grounds are also used

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.320
for other types of productions as well.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.460
The space behind us, this
big, open parking lot,

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.750
was used to look like
Afghanistan on CBS's "The Code."

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:26.937
Soldier: Where's my corpsman?

00:05:26.937 --> 00:05:28.230
Soldier: Cooper's dead, sir.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:30.296
He bled out on the way back.

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:31.947
Soldier: XStat on Adler's leg and call in

00:05:31.947 --> 00:05:33.237
for a dust-off now!

00:05:33.237 --> 00:05:35.010
Jake: And the swimming
pool has been converted

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:37.320
into a different type of soundstage,

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.080
one which can be used to
film underwater scenes.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.060
Filming at a place like Arthur
Kill instead of a studio

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.700
can make a show or film
seem all the more real

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.053
without breaking the bank.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.700
Just don't forget the
keys when you're putting

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.273
your actors behind bars.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.430
I would like a piece of cake,

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:57.720
but preferably if the cake
had a key baked into it

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.320
or maybe some kind of way
they can get me out of here

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.752
for the purpose of the scene I'm in.

00:06:01.752 --> 00:06:02.585
Thank you.

